<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Pricing</span>
<h1>Honda Click vs Honda Air Blade: Hanoi Rental Cost Comparison</h1>
<p>The Honda Click and the Honda Air Blade are two Hondas that live on opposite sides of the fleet's tier line. The Click is the entry-tier automatic, renting at verified rates of 150,000 VND per day, 700,000 VND per week, and 900,000 to 1,200,000 VND per month. The Air Blade is the step-up machine, renting at verified rates of 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week, and a flat 1,500,000 VND per month.</p>
<p>This guide compares those verified figures at every period, prices what the step-up premium buys, and pays special attention to the Air Blade's flat monthly rate, which changes the long-stay arithmetic in a way most comparisons miss. It builds on the guide to <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a>, the main <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> resource, and the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>. Numbers first, tier loyalty second.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">Two Hondas across a tier line</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">The verified rates side by side</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">What the premium pays for</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">The value case for the Click</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-5">The step-up case for the Air Blade</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-6">The flat month changes the math</a></li>
